align-items-center justify-content-center"></p><h3 id=soch>Soch</h3><h5 id=where-ideas-are-born>Where ideas are born.</h5><br><p>Everything starts with a thought, and that thought is your Soch.</p><p>This is the first round, where teams submit an abstract, a short write-up that
explains what your research idea is, why it is new or different, and why it
could matter in the real world. Think of it as your elevator pitch, only in a
written form. You do not need any fancy language. It simply needs to be clear
and impactful.</p><p>The abstract submission round is open to all undergraduates across any
department or college / institution. There is a wide variety of domains and
fields to choose from:</p><ul><li>Computer Science, AI & Data Science</li><li>Biosciences, Biotechnology & Healthcare</li><li>Chemistry & Chemical Engineering</li><li>Aerospace Engineering</li><li>Civil Engineering</li><li>Electrical, Electronics & Communication</li><li>Mechanical Engineering, Robotics & Automation</li><li>Physics, Mathematics & Materials Science</li><li>Environmental Science, Energy & Sustainability</li><li>Business, Entrepreneurship & Management</li></ul><p>The top teams advance to the next round, where they get the opportunity to
present their work at IIT Bombay.</p><p></div><div id=aboutvichar class="col col-12
align-items-center justify-content-center"></p><h3 id=vichar>Vichar</h3><h5 id=where-ideas-are-shared>Where ideas are shared.</h5><br><p>The second round is called Vichar, which translates to <strong>&ldquo;discussion&rdquo;</strong> or <strong>&ldquo;conversation&rdquo;</strong>.</p><p>Here, teams design a research poster, a single-page visual that explains their
research clearly, creatively, and engagingly. This is an online submission
round.</p><p>The poster should:</p><ul><li>Highlight your objectives, or what you are trying to achieve</li><li>Show your methodology, or how you are doing it</li><li>Share your key findings or progress so far</li><li>And most importantly, explain why it matters to the world</li></ul><p>Think of the poster as a blend of research, storytelling, and design. It should
be clear and engaging enough that even someone from a different field can
understand the essence of your work at a glance.</p><p>The top teams from the poster round move forward to the final presentation
stage.</p><br><a href=https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1ULurrk68tJgmCdxPYbb1YeOaMIsndQyf/ target=_blank aria-label=PPTX><i class="bi bi-filetype-pptx"></i><span class=t role=tooltip>PPTX: Poster template
</span>[Template]
</a>for posters !<br><p></div><div id=aboutachar class="col col-12
align-items-center justify-content-center"></p><h3 id=achar>Achar</h3><h5 id=the-grand-finale-presentation-round>The Grand Finale (Presentation Round).</h5><br><p>Finally, there is Achar, the final stage of ResCon, where teams bring together
their research, ideas, and presentation skills.</p><p>The top teams are invited to deliver a 15-minute presentation before a panel of
judges. This is where they get the full spotlight to share:</p><ul><li>What inspired their research</li><li>The goals of their work</li><li>Their approach to the problem</li><li>What they discovered or built</li><li>The significance of their work for industry, science, or society</li></ul><p>This round goes beyond presenting facts and slides. It is an opportunity for
teams to demonstrate the value and relevance of their research. The
presentation is followed by a Q&amp;A session with a panel of judges, who are
professors at IIT Bombay.</p><p></div></div></p><hr><br><br><h1 id=chief-guest-2025>Chief Guest (2025)</h1><br><p><div class="row align-items-center justify-content-evenly
